// ===========================================================================
// OBESITY — RECORDSET version. A complete, runnable policy.
//
// Height, Weight and BMI publish HISTORIES. They carry local codes, so they
// are assertable — but `shape is RecordSet` means they are NOT questions.
// Only `Obese` reduces to one record, so `Obese` is the single question, and
// the reduction happens at the TOP rather than at every level.
//
// ⚠ THE CONTRAST FIXTURE, and it is not optional. `shape is` is a
// DISCRIMINATOR, and a suite that only ever declares one value of it cannot
// notice when the discriminator is ignored. It also drives a different emitter
// path: a reduction over a local `shape is RecordSet` OPERAND is gated
// explicitly (`cql-emitter/emitCQL.ts`), so `BMI`'s operands here are
// RecordSets where the Record version's are Records.
//
// The two are alternative MODELS of one chain, not variants of one model —
// they generate different Questionnaires (four questions vs one). Which is
// canonical for the goal is an open question; both must keep working.
// ===========================================================================
library "Obesity Coverage (RecordSet)".

terminology "Obese VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/obese`.
terminology "Clinical BMI VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/bmi`.
terminology "Height VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/height`.
terminology "Weight VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/weight`.

// THE question, and the condition. `most recent` is concept-level: it spans
// BOTH arms — the threshold over the newest BMI, and existence of a coded
// Condition — selecting the one record this concept publishes.
concept "Obese":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `obese`.
- definition is "BMI" at least 30 'kg/m2', then most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is Condition.
  - coded from "Obese VS".
  - value projection is exists this.

// NOT a question — the local code makes it assertable, `shape is RecordSet`
// makes it a set. Its records are the UNION of the computed values (over the
// Height and Weight histories) and the recorded ones. A RecordSet publishes
// its set, so no reduction is owed.
concept "BMI":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `bmi`.
- definition is body mass index of "Weight" and "Height".
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Clinical BMI VS".

// NOT a question — a history of measurements.
concept "Height":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `height`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Height VS".

// NOT a question — a history of measurements.
concept "Weight":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `weight`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Weight VS".

activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `APPROVED`.

activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `NOT APPROVED`.

decision "Bariatric Surgery Coverage":
first:
- when "Obese" then recommend activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery".
